ehavior\n\nTests target supported library behavior. A known bug, regression, broken path,\nor version-specific failure is never asserted to make a call site \"covered\".\nException assertions are acceptable only for documented, supported\nnegative-path APIs, and no test name, comment, or assertion describes a broken\nbehavior path (\"fails before\", \"regression\", \"broken\"). If a call site is\nreachable only through broken behavior, it stays uncovered.\n\n```java\n// Bad: freezes a regression into the suite\n@Test void codecFailsSinceV5() {\n    assertThrows(NullPointerException.class, () -> codec.encode(message));\n}\n\n// Acceptable: a documented, supported negative path\n@Test void rejectsUnknownAlgorithm() {\n    assertThrows(IllegalArgumentException.class, () -> Codec.of(\"no-such-algo\"));\n}\n```\n"}], "isError": false, "timestamp": 1792548105193}, {"role": "toolResult", "toolCallId": "call_XNnHrS6RgBs1RI9n6o48F8QQ|fc_01254195ebacea78016ad81d08acec87d0bb94cdba67912842", "toolName": "read", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "        parser.parse(schema.toFile());\n\n        XSSchemaSet schemaSet = parser.getResult();\n        assertThat(schemaSet).isNotNull();\n        XSSchema ordersSchema = schemaSet.getSchema(\"urn:orders\");\n        assertThat(ordersSchema).isNotNull();\n\n        XSElementDecl order = ordersSchema.getElementDecl(\"order\");\n        assertThat(order).isNotNull();\n        assertThat(order.getType().isComplexType()).isTrue();\n\n        XSComplexType orderType = order.getType().asComplexType();\n        assertThat(orderType.getName()).isEqualTo(\"OrderType\");\n\n        XSModelGroup sequence = orderType.getContentType().asParticle().getTerm().asModelGroup();\n        assertThat(sequence.getCompositor()).isEqualTo(XSModelGroup.SEQUENCE);\n        assertThat(sequence.getSize()).isEqualTo(2);\n\n        XSElementDecl id = sequence.getChild(0).getTerm().asElementDecl();\n        assertThat(id.getName()).isEqualTo(\"id\");\n        asse